    Archived in its entirety therefore governs completeness of content, not sameness of bytes. Where a
    skipped element appears on one side it must remain a skipped element on the other. Where the tie
    breaking rule is paraphrased here the pre migration runtime is written JDK 8, a substitution that
    changes no meaning and that is disclosed rather than made silently. Read this record together with the
    coverage liveness note, jacoco-liveness.txt, in the migrated directory above: an empty coverage data
